    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwEQ",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Sir Timothy John Berners-Lee (born 8 June 1955),[1] also known as TimBL, is an English computer scie",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 473.390625,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 130,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwLA",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee proposed an information management system on 12 March 1989[5][6] and implemented the fir",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 619.390625,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 208,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwVw",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee was previously a senior researcher and holder of the 3Com founder's chair at the MIT Com",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 843.390625,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 286,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H2",
      "id": "Early_life",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Early life",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1160.390625,
      "w": 89.953125,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "\"Linux Libertine\", Georgia, Times, \"Source Serif 4\", serif",
      "fontSize": "24px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwjw",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee was born in London on 8 June 1955,[24] the son of the mathematicians and computer scient",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1203.46875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 130,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwnA",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee attended Sheen Mount Primary School, then Emanuel School (a direct grant grammar school ",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1349.46875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwrQ",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In 1976, Berners-Lee took a first in physics from The Queen's College, Oxford.[1][24] While there, h",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1443.46875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H2",
      "id": "Career_and_research",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Career and research",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1552.46875,
      "w": 190.546875,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "\"Linux Libertine\", Georgia, Times, \"Source Serif 4\", serif",
      "fontSize": "24px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "IMG",
      "id": "mwwA",
      "classes": "mw-file-element",
      "text": "",
      "x": 28,
      "y": 1605.546875,
      "w": 252,
      "h": 252,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwwg",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "After graduation, Berners-Lee worked as an engineer at the telecommunications company Plessey in Poo",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1595.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwzg",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee worked as an independent contractor at CERN from June to December 1980. While in Geneva,",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1689.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 104,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mw3A",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "After leaving CERN in late 1980, he went to work at John Poole's Image Computer Systems, Ltd, in Bou",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1809.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 104,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mw8A",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In 1989, CERN was the largest Internet node in Europe and Berners-Lee saw an opportunity to join hyp",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1929.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "I just had to take the hypertext idea and connect it to the TCP and DNS ideas and—ta-da!—the World W",
      "x": 56,
      "y": 1971.546875,
      "w": 888,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "— Tim Berners-Lee[31]",
      "x": 49.59375,
      "y": 2016.546875,
      "w": 194.0625,
      "h": 17,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Creating the web was really an act of desperation, because the situation without it was very difficu",
      "x": 56,
      "y": 2053.546875,
      "w": 888,
      "h": 104,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "— Tim Berners-Lee[32]",
      "x": 49.59375,
      "y": 2176.546875,
      "w": 194.0625,
      "h": 17,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "IMG",
      "id": "mwAQA",
      "classes": "mw-file-element",
      "text": "",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 2209.546875,
      "w": 252,
      "h": 189,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAQU",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee wrote his proposal in March 1989 and redistributed it in 1990. It then was accepted by h",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 2205.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 208,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwARY",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee published the first website, which described the project itself, on 20 December 1990; it",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 2429.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 130,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwASw",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In a list of 80 cultural moments that shaped the world, chosen by a panel of 25 eminent scientists, ",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 2575.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 104,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwATE",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In 1994, Berners-Lee founded the W3C at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology. It comprised vari",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 2695.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 104,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwATc",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee participated in Curl Corp's attempt to develop and promote the Curl programming language",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 2815.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAT0",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In 2001, Berners-Lee became a patron of the East Dorset Heritage Trust, having previously lived in C",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 2857.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAU8",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In a Times article in October 2009, Berners-Lee admitted that the initial pair of slashes (\"//\") in ",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 2951.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAVc",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Since 2021, Berners-Lee has been an advisory board member of Proton Foundation.[45]",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 3045.546875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H3",
      "id": "Policy_work",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Policy work",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 3101.140625,
      "w": 106.640625,
      "h": 21,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "19.2px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "IMG",
      "id": "mwAWA",
      "classes": "mw-file-element",
      "text": "",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 3144.65625,
      "w": 252,
      "h": 212,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAWM",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "By 2010, he created data.gov.uk alongside Nigel Shadbolt. Of the Ordnance Survey data in April 2010,",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 3135.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 156,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAWs",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In November 2009, Berners-Lee launched the World Wide Web Foundation (WWWF).[47]",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 3307.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "IMG",
      "id": "mwAXM",
      "classes": "mw-file-element",
      "text": "",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 3439.046875,
      "w": 252,
      "h": 169,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAXY",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee is one of the pioneer voices in favour of net neutrality,[48] and has expressed the view",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 3349.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 260,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAZA",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee was honoured as the \"Inventor of the World Wide Web\" during the 2012 Summer Olympics ope",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 3625.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 104,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "IMG",
      "id": "mwAag",
      "classes": "mw-file-element",
      "text": "",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 3757.859375,
      "w": 252,
      "h": 168,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAa8",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee joined the board of advisors of start-up State.com, based in London.[56] As of May 2012,",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 3745.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAbs",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "The Alliance for Affordable Internet (A4AI) was launched in 2013, and Berners-Lee is leading the coa",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 3839.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 156,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAcY",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee holds the founders chair in Computer Science at the Massachusetts Institute of Technolog",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 4011.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 130,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "IMG",
      "id": "mwAdw",
      "classes": "mw-file-element",
      "text": "",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 4169.859375,
      "w": 252,
      "h": 169,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAd8",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "From the mid-2010s, Berners-Lee initially remained neutral on the emerging Encrypted Media Extension",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 4157.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 286,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAgY",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "On 30 September 2018, Berners-Lee announced his open-source startup Inrupt to fuel a commercial ecos",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 4459.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAhI",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In November 2019, at the Internet Governance Forum in Berlin, Berners-Lee and the WWWF launched Cont",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 4553.859375,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 104,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H3",
      "id": "Awards_and_honours",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Awards and honours",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 4687.453125,
      "w": 190.484375,
      "h": 21,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "19.2px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "He wove the World Wide Web and created a mass medium for the 21st century. The World Wide Web is Ber",
      "x": 701.40625,
      "y": 4771,
      "w": 263.59375,
      "h": 160.125,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14.08px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAiU",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee has received many awards and honours. He was knighted by Queen Elizabeth II in the 2004 ",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 4752.96875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAjE",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "On 13 June 2007, he was appointed to the Order of Merit (OM), an order restricted to 24 living membe",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 4846.96875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 104,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAjc",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "He was elected a Fellow of the Royal Society (FRS) in 2001.[69] He was also elected as a member into",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 4966.96875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAkM",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "He has been conferred honorary degrees from a number of universities around the world, including Man",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5060.96875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 52,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAlQ",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In 2012, Berners-Lee was among the British cultural icons selected by artist Sir Peter Blake to appe",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5128.96875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAmE",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In 2013, he was awarded the inaugural Queen Elizabeth Prize for Engineering.[76] On 4 April 2017, he",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5222.96875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H2",
      "id": "Personal_life",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Personal life",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5331.96875,
      "w": 120.640625,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "\"Linux Libertine\", Georgia, Times, \"Source Serif 4\", serif",
      "fontSize": "24px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAm4",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee has said \"I like to keep work and personal life separate.\"[77]",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5375.046875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAnM",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee has married three times. Following final exams in Oxford, he married Jane Northcote (dau",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5417.046875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAno",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In 1990, Berners-Lee married Nancy Carlson, an American computer programmer. She was also working in",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5511.046875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 104,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwApA",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee was raised as an Anglican, but he turned away from religion in his youth. After he becam",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5631.046875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAps",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "The web's source code was auctioned by Sotheby's in London during 23–30 June 2021, as a non-fungible",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5725.046875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 52,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwArg",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In 2025, Berners-Lee published a memoir, This Is for Everyone, with ghostwriter Stephen Witt.[89] St",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5793.046875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 52,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAsc",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "In November 2025, Berners-Lee was the guest on BBC Radio 4's Desert Island Discs. His choices includ",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5861.046875,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H2",
      "id": "Views",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Views",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 5970.046875,
      "w": 59.890625,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "\"Linux Libertine\", Georgia, Times, \"Source Serif 4\", serif",
      "fontSize": "24px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAtc",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee views Wikipedia as probably the best single example of what he wanted the World Wide Web",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 6013.125,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 52,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAtw",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Wikipedia has grown to contain millions of articles on every subject known to our species – an inval",
      "x": 56,
      "y": 6081.125,
      "w": 888,
      "h": 78,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "mwAuI",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Berners-Lee is an advocate for a universal basic income.[93]",
      "x": 24,
      "y": 6183.125,
      "w": 952,
      "h": 26,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
